// fallow configuration (TICKET-DX-07, TICKET-DX-08)
//
// Three things fallow cannot see for itself once `src/` became three roots. Each is stated here
// rather than suppressed file by file, so that a *new* unused file is still a finding.
{
  // The TanStack Router plugin finds routes by convention at `src/routes/`, and DX-07 moved them
  // under the client root — `vite.config.ts` points the generator at `src/client` (D14). Without
  // these three lines the router entry, the generated tree and every route file drop out of the
  // reachability graph and are reported as dead code, which is a wrong answer about a live app.
  // `src/server/entry.ts` is named as a string in `vite.config.ts`
  // (`tanstackStart({ server: { entry } })`, TICKET-SRV-01) — the framework imports it, nothing
  // in the tree does.
  "entry": [
    "src/client/router.tsx",
    "src/client/routeTree.gen.ts",
    "src/client/routes/**/*.tsx",
    "src/server/entry.ts"
  ],

  // The modules that prove the architecture rules, dropped from fallow's analysis entirely
  // (TICKET-DX-08). Every one of them is a deliberate violation — an unimported file, an import
  // cycle, a devDependency in shipped code, a package absent from package.json — so fallow is
  // *right* about all of them and every finding is noise. What judges them is
  // `architecture/boundaries.test.ts`, which cruises `src/` with dependency-cruiser's own rules and
  // the fixture exemption lifted; see `architecture/README.md`.
  //
  // `ignorePatterns` rather than DX-07's `dynamicallyLoaded`, which only answered "is it
  // reachable" and left the dependency findings standing — and rather than `ignoreFindings`, which
  // cannot reach a *manifest*-owned finding such as `dev-dependency-in-production`.
  //
  // One glob rather than one per root, because DX-08's rules are scoped to directories *inside* a
  // root: a fixture has to live where the rule's `from` matches, which means under `shared/types/`
  // and under `client/components/ui/`, not only at a root.
  //
  // Nothing else loses coverage. Every module the fixtures import — `services/storage`,
  // `configStore`, the parser, the connection — has real consumers besides them.
  "ignorePatterns": ["src/**/boundaryFixtures/**"],

  // The route tree is **generated** by the TanStack router plugin and CLAUDE.md forbids editing it
  // by hand (TICKET-AUTH-01). It is a table of near-identical route entries, so every route added
  // makes it look more duplicated — a finding nobody can act on, against a file nobody may touch.
  // Scoped to clone detection: it stays an `entry` above, because the routes really do hang off it.
  "duplicates": { "ignore": ["src/client/routeTree.gen.ts"] },

  // `drizzle-kit` is a CLI (`yarn run db:generate`) and `drizzle.config.ts` is the file it reads;
  // neither is imported by anything in the tree.
  "ignoreDependencies": ["drizzle-kit"]
}
